<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=88862/tankiss-warstompers">
<img alt="Tankiss Warstompers" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_plate_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tankiss Warstompers</span></a></td>
<td>1750 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>
<br/>1750 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Protection Paladins</span></h2>Crafted gear is no longer profession locked for the most part, meaning even non-Blacksmiths can use Blacksmithing items. The main exceptions are <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77530/ghost-iron-dragonling">
<img alt="Ghost Iron Dragonling" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_head_dragon_bronze.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Iron Dragonling</span></a>  and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> , which still require their respective profession skills to be equipped. Crafted gear at 476 item level is ideal for pre-MSV gearing or as an affordable option afterwards, while the 496 versions will hold Pre-BiS status until you start raiding on Normal or Heroic difficulty.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> —  Overbudgeted for its level and it functions as a strong bonus cooldown in tight spots. A definite must-have in a Tanks repertoire.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> — Likely one the the best offensive trinkets on fights where you take little damage, purely on account of its item level. Might be prohibitively expensive and cannot be equipped simultaneously with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87406/gauntlets-of-battle-command">
<img alt="Gauntlets of Battle Command" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of Battle Command</span></a> — Solid option for defensive or hybrid setups. Slightly edges out <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a> for survivability, but the difference is marginal.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a> — A better pick for offensive and balanced sets, it is worth running if you're already comfortable with survivability.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87402/ornate-battleplate-of-the-master">
<img alt="Ornate Battleplate of the Master" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ornate Battleplate of the Master</span></a> — Mastery and Expertise make it a strong balanced piece. It edges out <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87405/unyielding-bloodplate">
<img alt="Unyielding Bloodplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unyielding Bloodplate</span></a> overall and is rightfully considered the Pre-BiS off-set item once Celestial dungeon tier sets can be acquired.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87405/unyielding-bloodplate">
<img alt="Unyielding Bloodplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unyielding Bloodplate</span></a> — Slightly more defensive than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87402/ornate-battleplate-of-the-master">
<img alt="Ornate Battleplate of the Master" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ornate Battleplate of the Master</span></a>, but not by a huge margin.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> — Extremely strong early on, thanks to customizable sockets. It loses some ground later but is still hard to beat and will likely remain BiS in Challenge Modes.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82979/breastplate-of-ancient-steel">
<img alt="Breastplate of Ancient Steel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breastplate of Ancient Steel</span></a> — Very solid stopgap if you can't afford crafted 496 items or the raid is yet to release. It edges out most dungeon options for raw mitigation.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82980/gauntlets-of-ancient-steel">
<img alt="Gauntlets of Ancient Steel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of Ancient Steel</span></a> — Similar use-case as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82979/breastplate-of-ancient-steel">
<img alt="Breastplate of Ancient Steel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breastplate of Ancient Steel</span></a> but likely more affordable, and it can be acquired before raids release.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> — Not amazing, but serviceable. Can fill in until better offensive trinkets drop. Use it if you're short on Valor or raid drops.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77530/ghost-iron-dragonling">
<img alt="Ghost Iron Dragonling" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_head_dragon_bronze.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Iron Dragonling</span></a> —  Does not stand out too much once you get access to Valor and Dungeon trinkets, but it remains one of the best trinkets once you decide to drop <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a>, as the sprockets are unique-equipped.</div></li></ul>
<div data-inserted-ad-group="2" style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; justify-content: center; align-items: center;">
<div data-ad="inline-leaderboard" data-multiformat="true" id="ad_inline-leaderboard_2" style="width: 728px; height: 250px; background: rgba(136, 136, 136, 0.133); --ad-width: 728px; --ad-height: 250px;">
<div data-house-ad="true" data-house-show-before-ad-request="" style="width: 728px; height: 90px;">
<a href="https://tidd.ly/4ckL1JD" target="_blank">
<img alt="ad" src="//r2.rev.iq/wowhead.com/House_BlizzGear_Apparel_728x90.webp"/></a></div></div></div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Protection Paladin Trinkets</span></h2>Trinkets play a key role in how you approach encounters, offering both defensive and offensive tools. Whether you prioritize survival, burst windows, or utility, choosing between passive bonuses, on-use effects, or procs lets you fine-tune your setup to suit the demands of your group and the challenge at hand.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Protection Paladins have a lot of flexibility in trinket choices and ideally bring a number of different options along with them to swap around at will.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> (Active) — A massive Dodge boost on a short cooldown. It is overbudgeted for its level and functions as a strong bonus cooldown in tight spots. A definite must-have in a Tanks repertoire.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89079/lao-chins-liquid-courage">
<img alt="Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage</span></a> (Active)  —  Mastery tends to be the most reliable defensive stat, making this trinket the next-best defensive option to use in fights where you feel pressured.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86775/jade-warlord-figurine">
<img alt="Jade Warlord Figurine" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_139.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jade Warlord Figurine</span></a> (Active) —  A slightly weaker version of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89079/lao-chins-liquid-courage">
<img alt="Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage</span></a>, except it can be bought with August Stone Fragments.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81243/iron-protector-talisman">
<img alt="Iron Protector Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Iron Protector Talisman</span></a> (Proc)  —  One of the better trinkets that can be acquired in Heroic Dungeons, the Stamina is solid and the Dodge proc is at least decent.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86881/stuff-of-nightmares">
<img alt="Stuff of Nightmares" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stuff of Nightmares</span></a> (Proc) —  This trinket offers less defensive utility than the Stamina counterparts, and it's long cooldown and unreliable proc make its value more of a gamble.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86790/vial-of-dragons-blood">
<img alt="Vial of Dragon's Blood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Dragon's Blood</span></a> (Proc)  —  A slightly lower-ilvl version of the other trinket. The shorter cooldown and weaker effect make it more reliable, but also less effective.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86894/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> (Proc) — This has a strong haste proc, and the passive Strength is serviceable, but the long cooldown and RNG timing reduce its reliability.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89083/iron-belly-wok">
<img alt="Iron Belly Wok" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_cooking_masterofthewok.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Iron Belly Wok</span></a> (Active) — Similar stats to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87172/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> but with an on-use effect, this is more predictable and better suited to planned pulls.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86771/jade-charioteer-figurine">
<img alt="Jade Charioteer Figurine" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_mount_ridinghorse.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jade Charioteer Figurine</span></a> (Active) —  A slightly weaker version of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89083/iron-belly-wok">
<img alt="Iron Belly Wok" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_cooking_masterofthewok.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Iron Belly Wok</span></a>, except it can be bought with August Stone Fragments.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86802/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a> (Proc) — High passive Haste is nice, but the Strength proc carries the same issues as other proc trinkets. Its lower cooldown and less powerful effect make it more reliable than its competition.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> (Proc) — Likely one the the best offensive trinkets on fights where you take little damage, purely on account of its item level. Might be prohibitively expensive and cannot be equipped simultaneously with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81268/lessons-of-the-darkmaster">
<img alt="Lessons of the Darkmaster" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lessons of the Darkmaster</span></a> (Active) — Good for reaching the Expertise cap, but the effect is underwhelming when actively tanking.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Protection Paladins</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit, whereas for Expertise the caps are split into 7.5% Expertise to reach the so-called "soft cap" and 15% Expertise to reach the true "hard cap." Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei racial Heroic Presence, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your melee hits no longer miss raid bosses. Spells, however, operate on a different Hit table and it would require additional investment into Hit to negate this miss chance entirely. In Mists of Pandaria, there exists another option: most Tanks will now look to solve their Spell Hit woes through Expertise.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to dodge your attack, but they can still parry them. For most raid encounters, you should aim to reach the full 15% Expertise cap to eliminate both dodge and parry from the equation. All gear sets recommended in this guide will meet this cap. There are exceptions, though—some raid bosses cannot parry, due to encounter mechanics or positioning. In those cases, it may be wise to reforge or swap gear to favor other stats.<br/>
<br/>Additionally, reaching 7.5% Expertise will also make you achieve Spell Hit cap, ensuring your spells such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=26573/consecration">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_innerfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Consecration</span></a> won't miss.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Protection Paladins</span></h2>Reaching the Expertise hard cap remains a top priority, and you'll often need to lean heavily on <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76693/precise-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Precise Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Primordial Ruby</span></a> to get there. Because of this, many of your early gem slots will be dedicated to pure Expertise, leaving limited room for alternatives. However, it's usually worth aiming for socket bonuses that grant Expertise, Hit, Haste, or Stamina in roughly that order of priority. To meet those bonuses efficiently, make use of hybrid gems, like <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76667/wicked-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Wicked Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wicked Vermilion Onyx</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76681/accurate-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Accurate Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Accurate Imperial Amethyst</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76642/lightning-wild-jade">
<img alt="Lightning Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning Wild Jade</span></a>. On certain fights with highly unpredictable spike damage, you may want to consider swapping in more <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76639/solid-rivers-heart">
<img alt="Solid River's Heart" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_blue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid River's Heart</span></a>  or <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a>, if your caps allow. Finally, keep in mind that <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76895/austere-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Austere Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Austere Primal Diamond</span></a> will always stick around as a meta gem option to increase your survivability, although <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a> will likely be the most common pick once you've geared up a bit.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76895/austere-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Austere Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Austere Primal Diamond</span></a> Defensive, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a> Offensive</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76693/precise-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Precise Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c7">Blue Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76636/rigid-rivers-heart">
<img alt="Rigid River's Heart" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_blue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid River's Heart</span></a> Balanced, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76639/solid-rivers-heart">
<img alt="Solid River's Heart" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_blue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid River's Heart</span></a> Defensive</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c4">Yellow Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76699/quick-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Quick Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Sun's Radiance</span></a> Balanced, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a> Defensive</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76667/wicked-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Wicked Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wicked Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
